# AVIATONLY Sales Pipeline CRM

Transform leads from a **flat data table** into a **workflow pipeline** — the primary seller CRM surface.

Related rules: `05-aviatonly-leads-offers-crm.mdc`, `08-aviatonly-lead-messaging-crm.mdc`, `01-aviatonly-listing-workflow.mdc`, `04-aviatonly-ui-rules.mdc`, `AGENTS.md`.

## How real CRMs work (HubSpot mental model)

AVIATONLY should follow **deal-centric** CRM, not contact-centric:

| HubSpot concept | AVIATONLY equivalent |
|-----------------|----------------------|
| Contact | Buyer (`User`) — profile, FICA, verification |
| Deal / Opportunity | **Lead** — buyer interest on **one listing** |
| Pipeline | Lead sales stages (`LeadStatus` columns) |
| Pipeline board | Kanban on `/dashboard/seller/leads` |
| Deal record page | `/dashboard/seller/leads/[leadId]` — drill-down, not the home screen |
| Inbox / sequences | `/dashboard/seller/messages` — conversation layer |

**Yes, per-record detail pages exist in the wild** — HubSpot opens a deal drawer/page when you click a card. You do **not** navigate CRM by picking a person first. You work the **pipeline**, then drill into a **lead (deal)** for actions, timeline, and messages.

A buyer with three aircraft enquiries = **three leads** (three cards), not one "CRM page per person".

## Current problem

- `/dashboard/seller/leads` is only `LeadsTable` — ops queue, not a sales workflow
- No visual pipeline; status is a table column
- Seller must hunt rows instead of seeing stage distribution and bottlenecks
- Lead detail workspace (`LeadWorkspace`) is correct but disconnected from how sellers should work day-to-day

**Messages** (`/dashboard/seller/messages`) stays the **inbox** for fast reply. **Pipeline** is for **stage management**. Both link to the same lead record.

## Product principles

- **Pipeline-first**: default view on seller leads is Kanban grouped by `LeadStatus`
- **Table is secondary**: keep `LeadsDataTable` as "List view" toggle for power users / export mindset
- **One card = one lead (deal)**: registration, buyer name, type, priority, last message preview, follow-up due, unread badge
- **Drag = server transition**: every column move calls a server action; `assertCanTransitionLeadStatus` in `lead-transitions.ts` is authoritative
- **Activity on every move**: `LeadActivity` `STATUS_CHANGED` row; never silent updates
- **Closed / unqualified off the board**: terminal stages in a "Closed" archive tab or collapsed column — not mixed with active pipeline
- **Aviation context on cards**: aircraft registration prominent; buyer verification badge; listing status chip when relevant

## Lead sales pipeline (Kanban columns)

Map existing `LeadStatus` to seller-facing columns (left → right):

```text
New          → NEW
Contacted    → CONTACTED
Qualified    → QUALIFIED
Viewing      → VIEWING_REQUESTED
Offer made   → OFFER_MADE
```

Side paths (not main columns):

- **Unqualified** → `UNQUALIFIED` (filter tab or single "Lost" bucket)
- **Closed** → `CLOSED` (archive view; requires `closedReason`)

Do **not** invent new statuses for Kanban without updating `lead-status.ts`, Prisma enum, `lead-transitions.ts`, and tests.

Optional auto-transitions (already partially implemented via messaging):

- First seller reply → `NEW` → `CONTACTED`
- Offer created → → `OFFER_MADE`

## Separate pipelines (do not merge into lead board)

Each workflow gets its own board or tab — same UX pattern, different domain:

| Pipeline | Stages (high level) | Primary route |
|----------|---------------------|---------------|
| **Lead / sales** | New → Contacted → Qualified → Viewing → Offer → Closed | `/dashboard/seller/leads` |
| **Listing onboarding** | Draft → Docs required → Under review → Approved → Live → Sold | `/dashboard/listings/[id]` workspace (or seller "My aircraft" pipeline later) |
| **Offers** | Received → Under review → Countered → Accepted / Rejected | `/dashboard/seller/offers` |
| **Auctions** | Scheduled → Live → Payment pending → Completed | auction admin/seller surfaces |

Build **lead pipeline first**. Reuse board primitives (`PipelineBoard`, `PipelineColumn`, `PipelineCard`) for offers second.

## Routes & navigation

```text
/dashboard/seller/leads                 → Sales pipeline (Kanban default + list toggle)
/dashboard/seller/leads/[leadId]        → Lead record (workspace) — opens from card click
/dashboard/seller/leads?view=list       → Explicit list view (optional URL state)
/dashboard/seller/leads?tab=closed      → Closed / archive
/dashboard/seller/messages              → Inbox (reply-first; link to pipeline card)
/dashboard/seller/offers                → Offer pipeline (Phase 2 of this rule)
```

Consider nav label **"Sales pipeline"** (subtitle: leads & enquiries) while keeping URL `/seller/leads` for stability.

## UI components (new — domain-specific)

Location: `src/components/dashboard/leads/pipeline/` (or `src/components/dashboard/pipeline/` if shared with offers)

| Component | Responsibility |
|-----------|----------------|
| `LeadPipelineBoard` | Columns from `OPEN_LEAD_STATUSES` + stage meta; horizontal scroll on mobile |
| `LeadPipelineColumn` | Header with count, drop zone, empty state |
| `LeadPipelineCard` | Compact deal card; click → detail page or `Sheet` drawer |
| `LeadPipelineToolbar` | View toggle (Board / List), filters (listing, priority, assignee), search |
| `LeadPipelineArchive` | Closed + unqualified leads table |

**DnD**: reuse `@hello-pangea/dnd` patterns from `dashboard/apps/kanban` — **not** `KanbanDataContext`, mock categories, or template task modals.

**Layout**: shadcn `Card`, `Badge`, `ScrollArea`, `Sheet` for mobile card detail; `gap-*` not `space-y-*`; no `section` tags in dashboard pages.

### Card content (minimum)

- Registration + aircraft title
- Buyer name + verification badge
- Lead type + priority
- Last message snippet + time (`lastMessageAt`)
- Unread indicator (seller read watermark)
- Follow-up overdue styling when `nextFollowUpAt` < now
- Quick actions: Open messages, Mark contacted (if allowed)

### Illegal drag handling

If `canTransitionLeadStatus(from, to)` is false: snap card back, `toast.error` with domain message. Optional confirm dialog when moving to `CLOSED` or `UNQUALIFIED` (require reason).

## Server layer

Add or extend in `src/lib/aviatonly/server/`:

| Function | Responsibility |
|----------|----------------|
| `queryLeadPipelineForSeller(scope)` | Group open leads by `status` for board payload |
| `transitionLeadStatusAction(leadId, toStatus, { reason? })` | Auth, transition assert, update lead, `LeadActivity`, revalidate |

Reuse `getLeadTableRows` for list view — do not duplicate query logic; share a base `querySellerLeads(scope, filters)`.

Drag-and-drop is **UI on top of the same server action** as `LeadWorkspaceActions` status buttons — one code path.

## Lead record page (keep, refine)

`/dashboard/seller/leads/[leadId]` remains the **deal record**:

- Header: stage badge (editable via actions), assignee, priority
- Tabs or sections: **Overview** | **Messages** (embed or link to inbox) | **Activity** | **Buyer** | **Aircraft**
- Actions sidebar: qualify, schedule viewing, convert to offer, set follow-up, close

Do **not** remove this page. Demote it from "how you browse CRM" to "what opens when you click a card".

## Admin pipeline

Mirror seller board at `/dashboard/admin/leads` with extra columns/filters:

- Unassigned queue
- Assign from card menu
- Cross-seller visibility

Admin uses same components with `showSeller` and broader scope.

## Anti-patterns (do not build)

- Flat table as the only seller CRM surface
- Contact-first CRM (`/dashboard/contacts/[userId]`) disconnected from listings
- Client-only Kanban with optimistic status and no server validation
- Wiring `dashboard/apps/kanban` context or mock task data into production routes
- One Kanban mixing leads, listings, and auctions
- Drag to `CLOSED` without `closedReason`
- Replacing lead detail workspace with only a message thread

## Recommended build order

```text
Phase 1 — Pipeline data & actions
  [ ] queryLeadPipelineForSeller (grouped by status)
  [ ] transitionLeadStatusAction (shared with workspace actions)
  [ ] Tests: illegal drag rejected; activity logged on move

Phase 2 — Seller board UI
  [ ] LeadPipelineBoard + Column + Card
  [ ] Replace seller leads page default with board + toolbar
  [ ] List view toggle reusing LeadsDataTable
  [ ] Card click → existing LeadWorkspace page

Phase 3 — Polish & ops
  [ ] Closed / unqualified archive tab
  [ ] Follow-up overdue highlights on cards
  [ ] Dashboard "Action required" pulls from pipeline (stale NEW, overdue follow-ups)
  [ ] Admin pipeline + assign from card

Phase 4 — Offer pipeline
  [ ] Reuse board primitives on /dashboard/seller/offers
  [ ] Offer status columns + link accepted offer → deal room

Phase 5 — Other pipelines (defer)
  [ ] Listing onboarding board on seller home or listings index
  [ ] Auction ops board
```

When the user says **"build sales pipeline"**, **"lead Kanban"**, or **"HubSpot-style CRM"**, start at Phase 1 unless they specify otherwise.

**Smallest vertical slice**: Phase 1 + Phase 2 with static columns and drag only between `NEW` ↔ `CONTACTED` ↔ `QUALIFIED` — then expand columns.

## Definition of done

1. Seller opens `/dashboard/seller/leads` and sees **Kanban by stage**, not only a table
2. Dragging a card updates status **server-side** with **audit trail**
3. Clicking a card opens the **lead record** with actions and messages
4. **List view** still available for search-heavy workflows
5. **Messages inbox** and **pipeline** stay in sync (same lead, two entry points)
6. Closed leads leave the active board

